On FreeBSD, all versions of LLVM from the ports tree are built against
the system libc++, which as of 2026-09-27 in the currently supported
releases is imported from LLVM 19. In this version, std::pair<> fails to
be constexpr-compatible in some cases where SpiderMonkey tries to use it.

The report about this upstream[1] was closed by the original author on
the basis that this is a problem with FreeBSD's libc++, not with
SpiderMonkey, and that it can be patched downstream.

This patch is adapted from the patch in the FreeBSD ports tree[1]. If
that patch is no longer present, this can be safely dropped.

[1] https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2038784
[2] https://cgit.freebsd.org/ports/tree/www/firefox-esr/files/patch-languageid-de-constexpr-ify

diff --git a/js/src/builtin/intl/CommonFunctions.h b/js/src/builtin/intl/CommonFunctions.h
index 2840286b9..b1c777698 100644
--- a/js/src/builtin/intl/CommonFunctions.h
+++ b/js/src/builtin/intl/CommonFunctions.h
@@ -58,7 +58,7 @@ extern void ReportInternalError(JSContext* cx, mozilla::intl::ICUError error);
  * an implementation, and that en-GB is more representative of the English used
  * in other locales.
  */
-static constexpr LanguageId LastDitchLocale() {
+static LanguageId LastDitchLocale() {
   return LanguageId::fromValidBcp49("en-GB");
 }
 
